// HIGH PRIORITY: Catch mathematical expressions before they get corrupted
// More specific patterns to avoid interfering with directory queries
+ whats # * #
- <call>handle_whats_expression <star1> <star2> <star3></call>

+ whats *#
- <call>handle_whats_expression <star></call>

+ whats #*
- <call>handle_whats_expression <star></call>

// Catch standalone mathematical expressions (like "2plus2", "5times3", etc)
+ *plus*
- <call>parse_attached_math <star1>plus<star2></call>

+ *minus*
- <call>parse_attached_math <star1>minus<star2></call>

+ *times*
- <call>parse_attached_math <star1>times<star2></call>

+ *divided*
- <call>parse_attached_math <star1>divided<star2></call>

+ what time is it
- The current time is <call>get_time</call>.

+ what date is it
- Today's date is <call>get_date</call>.

+ (calculate|math|compute) *
- <star> = <call>calculate <star></call>

+ what is # plus #
- <star1> + <star2> = <call>calculate <star1> + <star2></call>

+ what is # minus #
- <star1> - <star2> = <call>calculate <star1> - <star2></call>

+ what is # times #
- <star1> * <star2> = <call>calculate <star1> * <star2></call>

+ what is # divided by #
- <star1> / <star2> = <call>calculate <star1> / <star2></call>

// Handle contractions like "whats" with mathematical expressions
+ whats # plus #
- <star1> + <star2> = <call>calculate <star1> + <star2></call>

+ whats # minus #
- <star1> - <star2> = <call>calculate <star1> - <star2></call>

+ whats # times #
- <star1> * <star2> = <call>calculate <star1> * <star2></call>

+ whats # divided by #
- <star1> / <star2> = <call>calculate <star1> / <star2></call>

+ whats # divided #
- <call>parse_simple_math <star1> / <star2></call>

+ what is # divided #
